Qt 6.12.0 (qtdeclarative) fix #2: re-run the weak-value pass before marking ends
================================================================================

The incremental GC's weak-value pass (MarkWeakValues) walks all QObjectWrappers
once per cycle and marks those whose QObject - or the root of its parent chain -
keeps them alive (QQmlData::keepAliveDuringGarbageCollection: no QQmlData,
indestructible, or rootObjectInCreation). A QObject that becomes rooted AFTER
the pass ran in the current cycle (setParent() into a keep-alive chain, an
ownership change, rootObjectInCreation cleared on a chain root - all routine
while QML forms are built) keeps a wrapper the collector never marks: the
destroy phase tears it down and the sweep frees it while the QObject is still
alive and in use. Under real QML churn this crashes applications inside the
collector (QV4::MarkStack::drain); JASP ships installQmlGcRescan
(Desktop/utilities/qmlgcrescan.cpp) as a workaround for exactly this.

Fix: at MarkReady - after marking completed, before the destroy phase - re-run
InitMarkWeakValues + MarkWeakValues to completion (deadline suspended), then
hand back a fresh slice so InitCallDestroyObjects rescans the JS stack and
drains before anything is destroyed or swept. Only incremental runs can miss
anything (same guard as WeakValue::set's insertion barrier and as the
cross-validator's isIncrementalRun test).

Verified against a reproducer (QQmlEngine + component-created QML objects whose
wrappers are only weakly held, parented under a keep-alive anchor after a
randomized delay; QV4_GC_TIMELIMIT=1): an instrumented build that flags
wrappers destroyed while their QObject is rooted reports 25 missed wrappers per
run on unpatched 6.12.0 (3/3 runs) and 0 with this patch (3/3 runs), with the
rest of the GC behavior unchanged (JASPQuickTest identical to stock).

--- a/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
+++ b/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
@@ -751,11 +751,34 @@
 
-GCState markReady(GCStateMachine *that, ExtraData &)
+GCState markReady(GCStateMachine *that, ExtraData &extraData)
 {
     auto isIncrementalRun = [](GCStateMachine* that){
         return !that->mm->aggressiveGC && that->timeLimit.count() > 0;
     };
 
+    // Re-run the weak-value pass to completion before marking ends: a QObject
+    // that became rooted (parented into a keep-alive chain, ownership change,
+    // rootObjectInCreation cleared on a chain root) after this cycle's pass ran
+    // would otherwise keep a wrapper the collector never marks; the destroy
+    // phase tears it down and the sweep frees it while the QObject is still
+    // alive and rooted. The extra marks land on the mark stack;
+    // InitCallDestroyObjects rescans the JS stack and drains before anything is
+    // destroyed or swept. (The same guard as WeakValue::set's insertion
+    // barrier: only incremental runs can miss anything.)
+    if (that->mm->markStack() && that->mm->m_weakValues && isIncrementalRun(that)) {
+        that->deadline = QDeadlineTimer(QDeadlineTimer::Forever);
+        that->stateInfoMap[GCState::InitMarkWeakValues].execute(that, extraData);
+        while (that->stateInfoMap[GCState::MarkWeakValues].execute(that, extraData)
+               == GCState::MarkWeakValues) {}
+        // A fresh slice, so InitCallDestroyObjects (which redrains) runs before
+        // any JS can root more objects.
+        that->deadline = QDeadlineTimer(that->timeLimit);
+    }
+
     if (that->mm->crossValidateIncrementalGC && isIncrementalRun(that))
         return GCState::CrossValidateIncrementalMarkPhase;
     return GCState::InitCallDestroyObjects;
 }
